==English==
{{Wikiquote}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fa|en}} {{term|مجاهد|lang=fa|tr=mujáhid}}, and its source, {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|مجاهد|lang=ar|tr=mujáhid}}, active participle of {{term|جاهد|lang=ar|tr=jāhada||to wage holy war}} (verbal noun: {{term|جهاد|lang=ar|tr=jihād||holy war as a religious duty}}), from the root {{ar-root|ج|ه|د}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/mʊˈdʒɑːhɪd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|mujahideen}}

# {{context|Islam|lang=en}} A Muslim engaging in [[jihad]], especially armed jihad; a [[jihadist]].

====Synonyms====
* [[jihadist]], [[jihadi]]
* {{sense|struggler for Islam}} [[Quran thumper]], [[Koran thumper]], [[Koran basher]], [[takfiri]]

